**Structure** (m4, 15 min, Polish prose / English technical terms, ~0.5 theory/practice):
`theory → quiz → code → theory → dataTable → plotImage → sandbox` (2 theory beats + 5 widgets; starts on theory, no back-to-back theory, ends on a widget).
1. **Predict mode** (theory) — running inference, the `conf` vs `iou` thresholds, the `Results` object; inline pipeline diagram.
2. **Quiz** — diagnoses the conf-vs-iou-threshold misconception (duplicate boxes → lower NMS IoU).
3. **Code** — `unletterbox_box(...)`: rescale detections from the 640×640 letterbox grid back to original-image pixels (pure Python, 1 visible smoke test + 3 hidden, full reference solution; all four verified passing).
4. **Export** (theory) — `model.export()`, ONNX as a portable interchange format, TensorRT as the compiled NVIDIA engine; inline export-flow diagram.
5. **DataTable** — six export formats (torchscript/onnx/engine/openvino/coreml/tflite) × file / runtime / when-to-use.
6. **PlotImage** — example inference latency per format (PyTorch/ONNX/TensorRT FP16) with full axes/labels/title.
7. **Sandbox** — convert latency → FPS and compute speedup.
**Sources:** 4 lesson-level entries copied wholesale from `sources.md` (Ultralytics Predict/Export, ONNX, NVIDIA TensorRT), plus section-level sources on both theory beats and the two reference widgets.
